# TEMPLATE: a card a knight finds (in a chest, from a monster) and keeps.
# Copy this file, then change what it says. Check it with
#   cargo run -p angel-delve --example content_check -- <your file>
# and add it to cockpit/assets/dungeon/cards/ and `cards::BUILTIN` when it passes.
#
# Change: name (at most 22), kind (take, hold, play, arm, guard or spell),
#   rarity (common, rare, relic), text (one line of what it does, at most 64),
#   its effects (at most 3, from `/dungeon cards`), the art.
# Keep: numbers inside their ranges (a number past one is held to it, and the
#   card says so: write the number the game will use); `drop` and `chest` only
#   to weigh it off its rarity's own.
# The bar: its art Fine or better (a template, Masterwork), up to 16 by 16:
#   one silhouette, a dark edge, 4 to 6 inks shaded dark to light.
name   Hunter's Whetstone
kind   hold
rarity common
text   An edge kept keen: every shot and swing bites a little deeper.
damage 8
art
